00:03:49.467 --> 00:03:54.707
knows more, and how it works is a wider spread plus a price that jumps once that order teaches

00:03:54.707 --> 00:03:59.827
the book something. The person who has seen what the maker has not buys the cheap side and sells

00:03:59.827 --> 00:04:04.847
the rich side. The maker is the one who loses the fill. In the studies that follow,

00:04:04.847 --> 00:04:09.507
below, the reply is to charge uninformed flow enough to cover those losses, and to

00:04:09.507 --> 00:04:14.047
step the quote away after an order that carries news, because the order is the news.

00:04:14.587 --> 00:04:19.747
An archive paper, market informiveness, and market maker profitability builds a market

00:04:19.747 --> 00:04:23.987
where makers differ in what they know and in how hard they try to avoid inventory.

00:04:24.707 --> 00:04:28.627
Prices are made inside the market, a fundamental wanders on its own.

00:04:29.247 --> 00:04:33.127
Takeer orders are self-exciting, so one burst makes the next more likely.

00:04:33.127 --> 00:04:38.767
The authors show that flow stays stable over a finite horizon, then train the makers with

00:04:38.767 --> 00:04:42.947
multi-agent reinforcement learning, shared training, and separate execution.

00:04:43.507 --> 00:04:48.207
When few participants are informed, an informed taker can hit a quote that has not moved,

00:04:48.607 --> 00:04:51.067
and the maker cannot tell that order from noise.

00:04:51.627 --> 00:04:56.747
The paper finds that kind of flow, especially damaging, with severe adverse selection risk.

00:04:57.267 --> 00:05:01.547
Lift how much of the market is informed, and more orders already carry the fundamental,

00:05:01.547 --> 00:05:07.227
so endogenous prices move with them. A late quote can still be picked off, but it is late

00:05:07.227 --> 00:05:12.747
by less, and the maker's other fills sit closer to what is known. Profitability then trends

00:05:12.747 --> 00:05:18.787
up overall. The path bends back in places, from messy dynamics and from learning that is itself

00:05:18.787 --> 00:05:24.627
random. The authors read that as price discovery paying for the cost of being picked off. A second

00:05:24.627 --> 00:05:30.827
archive paper, when AI trading agents compete, trains a fast maker with reinforcement learning inside

00:05:30.827 --> 00:05:35.167
a hawks order book model, so impact comes from the book rather than from a

00:05:35.167 --> 00:05:40.247
formula someone assumed. The maker does not reprice on every tick. The job is

00:05:40.247 --> 00:05:45.067
impulse control, trained with proximal policy optimization and self-imitation.

00:05:45.647 --> 00:05:49.927
Set against a slower trader working a large order in pieces, the maker learns

00:05:49.927 --> 00:05:54.427
to use the drift that sliced order creates. The quote moves because of the order.

00:05:54.967 --> 00:05:58.547
That move is the book learning who is trading. Bigger profits for the

00:05:58.547 --> 00:06:02.587
learning maker did not necessarily mean much larger slippage for the slower one.

00:06:03.087 --> 00:06:07.967
Inform trading intensity in the Journal of Finance is a machine learning measure trained

00:06:07.967 --> 00:06:09.707
on a class of informed trades.

00:06:10.147 --> 00:06:14.507
It rises before earnings, before mergers and acquisitions, and before news.

00:06:15.067 --> 00:06:19.627
The author's tie it to return reversal and to asset pricing, and say it works because

00:06:19.627 --> 00:06:25.127
it catches non-linear ties among informed trading, volume, and volatility, including

00:06:25.127 --> 00:06:29.727
Impatient informed trading and informed trading that shows up in common across names.

00:06:30.287 --> 00:06:35.347
A journal of financial and quantitative analysis study of options around stock split announcements

00:06:35.707 --> 00:06:39.147
finds traders do expect volatility to rise after a split.

00:06:39.767 --> 00:06:44.507
Evidence they also expect an abnormal jump in the share price is only weak, and there

00:06:44.507 --> 00:06:48.267
is little evidence those option measures forecast the splitting firms returns.

00:06:48.967 --> 00:06:53.067
A quote can learn that uncertainty changed and still be a poor read on direction.

00:06:53.067 --> 00:06:58.007
A sharp step after a single order is the book revising who it thinks just traded.

